```
http {
    ...
    server {
        listen 199.2.31.2:9938;
        server_name my_user_gfw;

        auth_basic on;
        auth_basic_user_file /path/to/users.txt;

        if ($remote_addr = 199.2.31.2) {
            return 200;
        }

        error_page 401 = /SSL SOCKET ERROR 443:ERN;
    }
}
```
This configuration listens on port 9938 and expects the username and password to be sent in the `Authorization` header. If the credentials are valid, the server returns a 200 OK response. If the credentials are invalid, the server returns a 401 Unauthorized response.

